# 35. What Is Saturated?

These concepts aren't dead.

But I would not rely upon them alone.

### "Perfect husband has a secret"

Extremely familiar.

### "Woman moves into beautiful house where something happened"

Needs another hook.

### "Alcoholic woman sees something through window"

Very familiar.

### "Group of friends reunite and someone dies"

Needs distinctive environment/history.

### "Woman wakes with no memory"

Needs unusual mechanism.

### "Rich family has dark secrets"

What secrets?

### "Influencer isn't who she seems"

Needs specific threat.

### "Nanny enters creepy household"

Still effective, heavily used.

### "Therapist knows dangerous secret"

Still useful, familiar.

### "Everyone on vacation is lying"

Needs a strong differentiator.

The problem is not using these tropes.

The problem is believing the trope itself is your premise.

